 ```
 
+`createPatch(from, to)` creates an RFC 6902 patch that changes `from` into
+`to`, without changing or retaining references to either input. It recursively
+describes changed object members and uses indexed edits for arrays, so a small
+change does not require sending the entire document. The generated patch uses
+`add`, `remove`, and `replace` operations and can be passed to `applyPatch`.
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch, createPatch } from "json-toolkit";
+
+const before = { profile: { name: "Ari", nickname: "A" } };
+const after = { profile: { name: "Arianna" } };
+const patch = createPatch(before, after);
+
+// [
+//   { op: "remove", path: "/profile/nickname" },
+//   { op: "replace", path: "/profile/name", value: "Arianna" },
+// ]
+applyPatch(before, patch); // { profile: { name: "Arianna" } }
+```
+
